From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:40:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] VICTORY_CAPTURE_LATE=1: a saved frame keeps the free
 present

Off by default: a frame that is saved is presented the old way, as
before. With the switch, a frame saved for its picture alone is sent
ahead like every other present (late_free_present); its picture is
copied into a read-back buffer inside that flight and written out by a
thread of ours ("victory frame saver") once the card has run the
flight: the mapping, the half-size picture, its compression and the
file are that thread's work. Listed frames (VICTORY_CAPTURE_FRAMES, the
world's frames, a trigger's) keep the old way: their operations and
targets are written too.

Why: a saved frame's present settled every flight in the air and read
the frame back at once, holding the submission lock meanwhile. With a
picture of every second frame the submitting thread waited 64 to 83 ms a
frame for that lock, and 64 to 145 ms with a picture of every frame
(run 66), in frames of 270 to 420 ms.

Not tested beyond compiling and the existing tests: what it does shows
only in a run (pictures still arriving for every saved frame; the
"waiting for the submission lock" figure). A flight that has not
finished after ten seconds is given up on and said in the log.

victory-gpu: 154 passed (163 with diagnostics), 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 355746e0724594bbb748a4d768e2367cbb6065b2)
